      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FLYING DUCATI (8) was quickly out of the boxes with a slick early sectional clocking 30.77 with a 5.5 lengths win at Ballarat over 545m. Form is hard to fault from this box, with a win and five minor placings from six starts. Can make it back-to-back wins. JUNGLE JOHNNY (2) has been settling off the speed lately, finishing sixth (30.17) last time in a S/E Group 1 at The Meadows. Has a strong record out of this box with four wins and two minor placings from 10 starts. Should be thereabouts. BALLYMAC IROKO (1) improved his time on first attempt this course and distance with a neck win in 29.59 here latest. Expected to feature again. PAW WINDER (7) was well supported last time but could only manage second (29.62), beaten a neck. Deserves a win and gets his chance.",
